invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont_division.h
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: the division by which a host object's rsa_vp1 multiplies the base
  by R divides the remainder's top two words by the modulus's top word
  even when the remainder's top word equals the modulus's, where the
  quotient passes 2^64 and its low word is no estimate. No random
  signature meets that step. bin/rsa_equiv_test's signature n - 1 does,
  under every modulus, and its answers then differ from the 32-bit arm's.
  The entry was named for the division of R^2, which decision 208
  replaced with this one.

--- old
    if (top < m[k - 1]) {
        estimate = (uint64_t)((((ct_u128)top << 64) | rem[k - 2]) / m[k - 1]);
--- new
    if (1) {
        estimate = (uint64_t)((((ct_u128)top << 64) | rem[k - 2]) / m[k - 1]);
